{"name":"Cinderella","hex":"#fbd7cc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cinderella","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A popular fairy tale embodying a classic folk tale myth-element of unjust oppression and triumphant reward.","The main character in this story, a mistreated and impoverished girl."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mistreated and impoverished girl.","Something rising unexpectedly from obscurity to success, as a Cinderella team."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cinderella"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cinderella","blocks":[{"text":"Cinderella is a folk tale with thousands of variants that are told throughout the world. The protagonist is a young girl living in unfortunate circumstances who is suddenly blessed with remarkable fortune, ultimately ascending to the throne through marriage. The earliest known version of the Cinderella story is usually considered to be the Greek story of Rhodopis, as described by the scholar Strabo sometime between 7 BC and 23 AD, about a Greek slave girl who marries the king of Egypt."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Cendrillon.jpg/330px-Cendrillon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinderella"},{"title":"Cinderella (1950 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cinderella is a 1950 American animated musical fantasy film produced by Walt Disney Productions and released by RKO Radio Pictures. Based on Charles Perrault's 1697 fairy tale, the film follows Cinderella, the daughter of a widowed aristocrat, who is forced to become a servant of her cruel stepmother and two stepsisters, until Cinderella's fairy godmother grants her the chance to attend the royal ball and meet the prince. The production was supervised by Ben Sharpsteen, and was directed by Wilfred Jackson, Hamilton Luske, and Clyde Geronimi. It features the voices of Ilene Woods, Eleanor Audley, Verna Felton, Rhoda Williams, June Foray, James MacDonald, and Luis van Rooten."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/1950_is_the_Cinderella_year.jpg/330px-1950_is_the_Cinderella_year.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cinderella_(1950_film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Marie_de_France_1.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Marie_de_France_1.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Marie_de_France_1.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Marie_de_France_1.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Marie_de_France_1.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Marie_de_France_1.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration of Marie de France, the author of Le Fresne, from a medieval illuminated manuscript","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMarie_de_France_1.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Giambattista_Basile_by_Nicolaus_Perrey.jpg/500px-Giambattista_Basile_by_Nicolaus_Perrey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Giambattista_Basile_by_Nicolaus_Perrey.jpg/500px-Giambattista_Basile_by_Nicolaus_Perrey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Italian author Giambattista Basile wrote the first literary version of the story.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGiambattista_Basile_by_Nicolaus_Perrey.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Stories_from_the_Pentamerone-0088.jpg/500px-Stories_from_the_Pentamerone-0088.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wi